  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.14.0: GetAsync, PeekAsync, QueryAsync, SearchAsync and CountAsync go again after an answer 429, 500, 502, 503 or 504, a request that fails on the network, or an answer whose lists do not have one item for every record, with the exponential backoff with full jitter of AWS: by default 4 attempts at most, a base delay of 50 ms and a largest delay of 1 second. A write never goes again. New: ChromaReadRetries, with Default, None, MaxAttempts, BaseDelay and MaxDelay, and ChromaConfigurationOptions.ReadRetries and WithReadRetries; ChromaReadRetries.None keeps the behavior of 2.13.0. An uneven answer that stays throws a ChromaException instead of an ArgumentOutOfRangeException. All the releases: https://github.com/ChromaDotNet/ChromaDB.Client/releases. Tested versions: https://github.com/ChromaDotNet/ChromaDB.Client/blob/main/docs/COMPATIBILITY.md. Migration from 1.x: https://github.com/ChromaDotNet/ChromaDB.Client#migrating-from-chromadbclient-1x",
